course: dictionary
lesson: 10756
title: Formal and everyday words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are for everyday talk, and some are for doctors and science books. «Urinate» is the formal word. It means to pass urine, the body's wee, out of the body. Everyday people often say «wee» or «pee» instead.
explain: The word changes shape like other verbs: urinates, urinated, urinating. «The doctor asked how often he needed to urinate.» The clues are doctor and how often, so this is a serious, medical sentence, not a chatty one.
explain: Context shows you what kind of word you are reading. «Number one» and «take a leak» are slang, and «relieve oneself» is polite. They can all point to the same thing, but each has a different feeling. Choose the word that fits the people and place you are talking about.
fact: Urinate means to pass urine out of the body.
fact: The body gets rid of waste water and salts this way. The kidneys make them into urine, which is stored in the bladder until we urinate.
fact: «Wee» is the everyday British word, and «pee» is the everyday word in the USA.
fact: «Relieve oneself» is a polite phrase that can mean urinate or poo.
fact: In health, needing to urinate a lot, or feeling pain when you do, is something to tell a doctor about.
exercise: The doctor asked, «How often do you need to urinate?» What does urinate mean? | To wash your hands | *To pass urine out of the body | To feel sleepy after lunch | To drink lots of water
exercise: Which everyday word for a wee is used in Britain? | pee | urinate | bladder | *wee
exercise: Find and copy one polite phrase from the lesson that can mean urinate or poo. | take a leak | number one | *relieve oneself | wee
test: Which word is the polite, scientific word that doctors use? | *urinate | wee | pee | leak
test: Why is «take a leak» different from «urinate»? | It means something completely different | It is a longer word | It only means poo | *It is informal and chatty, while urinate is formal
exam: Which sentence uses urinate in the right way? | We urinate our dinner before school | *Needing to urinate often can be something to tell a doctor about | The bus will urinate at the station | Urinate is a colour of the sky
